# Everything is excluded first, then only what the Dockerfile copies is added back.
# A denylist would have to be extended for every new file, and the one it would miss is
# `.env`: it sits in the repository root, holds real credentials, and reaches the build
# daemon — and every build stage — the moment it is part of the context.
#
# The cost of the allowlist is that a new COPY needs a line here. That failure is a build
# error, which is the right way round: loud when something is missing, never silent when
# something secret is present.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json

!src
!templates
!public
